    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2506.04087v1</id>
    <title>Close points on a modular hyperbola</title>
    <updated>2025-06-04T15:46:15Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.04087v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.04087v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In this paper, we continue the study of small squares containing at least two points on a modular hyperbola $x y \equiv c \pmod{p}$. We deduce a lower bound for its side length. We also investigate what happens if the ``distances" between two such points are special type of numbers like prime numbers, squarefree numbers or smooth numbers as well as more general multiplicatively closed sets or almost dense sets.</summary>
